# opencode — ported from the opencode TUI theme.
#
# Source: anomalyco/opencode @ 10765ff, packages/tui/src/theme/assets/opencode.json
#
# That file defines *semantic* UI colors (primary, syntaxKeyword, error, ...)
# over a 12-step neutral ramp, not the 16 ANSI slots a terminal needs. The six
# named hues (Red/Green/Yellow/Secondary/Accent/Cyan) map onto ANSI 1-6, the
# neutral ramp supplies black/white, and the missing half of each pair is
# derived by a lightness nudge of -0.09 with saturation +0.03 -- the mean
# normal->bright delta measured across VS Code's own dark palette.
#
# Regenerate by re-reading opencode.json and re-applying that mapping.

# Light variant. ANSI 1-6 are opencode's own hues; 9-14 are derived darker,
# since a lighter 'bright' would wash out against the white background.

